    "longest_thought": "The key threat is Garchomp at 16% HP on the bench. Raging Bolt is Electric-typed, so it takes super-effective Earthquakes from Garchomp. If the opponent switches to Garchomp, I'd be forced to take a super-effective hit or switch. Earthquake is super effective against Kleavor (Bug/Rock) and would likely KO it, but Kleavor is just a setup sweeper. The real danger is Garchomp coming in. I should use Calm Mind to boost and threaten, keeping options open, rather than committing. Actually, Earthquake KO's Kleavor and I can then deal with Garchomp, but Raging Bolt would be weakened. Safer to Calm Mind and force the switch.",
